  "prompts": {
    "run.txt": "You write a short decodable early-reader story book for one reviewed cumulative phonics stage. Dialect is en-US only. Stage vocabulary is the hard boundary: every child-visible title, heading, and prose word must be decodable within the selected stage's reviewed cumulative vocabulary or appear on the reviewed sight-word list, except the optional child's name, which is the sole special-word exception and is never represented as stage-decodable. The theme is inspiration only, not permission to introduce out-of-stage vocabulary; very early stages may adapt the theme to a fluent stage-safe motif and omit topic words the child has not reached. Keep at least three story sections and enough prose for a useful short book. Do not claim diagnosis, intervention, curriculum alignment, grade mastery, or suitability for any particular learner. Do not deliver a draft that still contains out-of-stage words; adapt the motif instead of deleting words into broken prose. Return exactly one JSON object with keys title (string), book (Markdown string with at least three sections), and page_plan (array of 3-14 concise strings). Do not include markdown fences or commentary outside the JSON object."
  },
  "readiness": {
    "blockers": [
      {
        "code": "DECODABILITY_VOCABULARY_MISSING",
        "detail": "The reviewed OSS contract requires every child-visible word to pass a compiler-owned stage vocabulary plus a reviewed sight-word list, recomputed deterministically, and a runnable result must contain no review words. MACHINERY IS DONE (2026-08-16): the compiler now has the semantic.whole_book_vocabulary/v1 kind (selector + deterministic whole-book token classifier + decodability report recompute in the generated runtime), fixture-proven 3/3 with clearly-labeled SYNTHETIC vocabulary (right needle, out-of-stage word, unknown stage) and fail-closed selection until a reviewed vocabulary resource is bound. The ONLY missing part is the REVIEWED CONTENT: the five cumulative stage vocabularies + sight-word list. Verified exhaustively this tick that no reviewed word-list source exists anywhere: the OSS twin publishes only SKILL.md/README/LICENSE/manifest per skill (no data files), every PhonicsMaker inventory skill is a procedural generator with no static word bank, and this repo has no third-party corpora. Resume: Harry supplies or signs off the five stage lists + sight-word list (or names a source), bind them as reviewed_spec.vocabulary in the profile, regenerate the container, flip can_submit. The paper price ($0.99) and schemas are reviewed and stay fixed."
      }
    ],
    "can_submit": false
  },
